# THE AI GATEWAY'S LOCAL SETTINGS — an EXAMPLE (BE-W204). The real file is `.env`, beside this one.
#
#   1. Copy this file to `services/api/supabase/functions/.env` (git-ignored: `.gitignore`, line 3).
#   2. Put the real key in `.env` with an EDITOR. NEVER `echo ... >> .env`: if the file has no final
#      newline, echo glues the new setting onto the last one and BOTH break, silently
#      (docs/START-HERE.md, Trap 4). Never paste the file's contents into a chat, an issue or a log.
#   3. Start (or restart) `pnpm functions:serve` AFTER saving it — the function reads it at start.
#   4. Check it: `pnpm ai:live` (docs/KEY-DAY.md says what "it worked" looks like).
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Nothing in this file is a secret: the key below is a placeholder.
# Production does NOT read this file: there the same names are Edge Function secrets, set by the
# operator in the Supabase dashboard (docs/KEY-DAY.md, "Production").

# Which vendor answers. `openai` is the pilot's (BE-C79). Unset (or anything else) = the labelled
# practice STUB, which refuses any non-local target — CI and the ordinary test suites rely on that.
AI_PROVIDER=openai

# The OpenAI secret key ("sk-..."). Replace the placeholder in `.env`, never here.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE-ME-in-.env-never-in-this-file

# --- The alternative: Amazon Bedrock, India (BE-C26, kept). Use INSTEAD of the two lines above:
# AI_PROVIDER=bedrock
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=REPLACE-ME
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=REPLACE-ME
# AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
